---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getApp, COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('shopkeep')!;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${app.name} Support — ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description="Help with ShopKeep sign-in, private photos and documents, account deletion, inventory exports, and the current native release state."
  path="/shopkeep/support"
  noindex={true}
  socialImage="/apps/shopkeep.png"
  socialImageAlt="ShopKeep app icon"
>
  <article class="prose container">
    <a class="back-link" href="/shopkeep">← {app.name}</a>
    <h1>{app.name} Support</h1>

    <p class="callout">
      <strong>Current availability.</strong> ShopKeep has a working web app and a
      private native pre-release build. There is no public App Store listing,
      TestFlight acquisition link, or announced price.
    </p>

    <h2>Get direct help</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> with the
      device or browser, ShopKeep version when known, sign-in provider, and the
      steps that led to the problem. Do not send passwords, verification codes,
      access tokens, payment details, or private inventory files unless support
      explicitly asks for a redacted example.
    </p>

    <h2>Apple and Microsoft sign-in</h2>
    <p>
      Apple and Microsoft create separate ShopKeep accounts, even when both
      providers use the same email address. Confirm which provider you used
      before assuming inventory is missing. Signing out and choosing the other
      provider opens that provider’s separate account.
    </p>

    <h2>Photos and documents</h2>
    <p>
      Tool photos and attached documents require an authenticated account
      request. If media stops loading, confirm the account session is active,
      retry on a stable connection, and avoid sharing the raw request URL: it is
      not a public file link.
    </p>

    <h2>Delete a ShopKeep account</h2>
    <p>
      In the native app, open <strong>Settings → Account &amp; Data</strong>,
      review the deletion summary, and confirm <strong>Delete ShopKeep
      Account</strong>. The app signs out only after the backend confirms
      deletion. A failure leaves the account active and shows a recovery action;
      do not assume a failed request removed data.
    </p>
    <p>
      Deletion applies only to the selected Apple or Microsoft ShopKeep account.
      It does not delete the provider account or a ShopKeep account made with the
      other provider.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Read the <a href="/shopkeep/privacy/">ShopKeep Privacy Policy</a> for
      details about account data, private media, AI processing, retention, and
      deletion.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
